On Wednesday 09 October 2002 16:53, Dave Pomeory wrote:
> My business has a web page that uses javascript.  I can't seem to make it
> work in Mozilla, Netscape, or Korqurer.  When I boot into windows and use
> Internet Exployer it works fine.  Anyone have a clue as to what is going
> on?  Do I need a plugin for Javascript?  Thanks for your help. Mandrake 9.0

I don't know which distribution you are running or if you previously installed 
java or not. I do know that none of the major distributions come with java 
installed because it is not public domain.

You may acquire java for linux here:

http://java.sun.com/j2se/1.4.1/

After you install java you must also make all the links to all the programs 
that use java or the programs will not be able to find it.

Be prepaired to spend some tine doing the down load. I have done it over a 56 
K modem actually running about 48 K in just under 12 hours and I failed to do 
it tonight using someone else's T3 line in a hour and a half.

Thanks

